report=f'''Independent corrected r38 generation review — PASS for sampled checks\n\n1024 attempted / 1024 successful complete 40-floor worlds ; 40960 populated floors; zero generation errors, invariant failures, panics or substitute seeds. Eight fixed seed families. Each checks admission, floor count, planned domain/Godbeast identity, accepted quality/bounds, hazard-free cardinal stair accessibility, portal/non-Euclidean topology, biome validity, legal nonoverlapping actors/items, and required tap/dagger/shards/Sphinx rewards/Zillennia. Sixteen diverse worlds regenerate exactly and save/load compare. Separate 32 Blessed and 32 Avatar worlds pass the same suite, including explicit 0-1-2 and 9-10-11 prefixes.\n\nThe same baseline r37 corpus had 1017 successes / 7 generation failures: six tap/stair collisions and one inaccessible-room abort. All seven pass separate corrected regressions. The first r38 candidate generated 1024 worlds but failed hazard-free cardinal-route checks in five. Those late-habitat defects were not suppressed: source was corrected and all 1024 rerun from scratch. All five also pass a separate targeted run. Eight-way runtime movement can still offer paths in the minimized pre-fix case; do not describe every old case as unplayable.\n\nTen revisions 29–38 each generate a repeatable 40-floor world and roundtrip. Nine historical 29–37 serialized worlds are byte-identical SHA256 to frozen r37 output. Sixteen DEBUG cases compare true prior heart count and untouched target actors/loot to normal worlds, complete earned choices, admit Engine and execute deterministic Wait after load. Exact heart-audit-000071 succeeds through 40 floors and DEBUG 27. Four extra worlds preserve encounter heart budgets, four Nightmares/floor and finale boss. Thirty-two extra worlds pass full generation validation and every ground item is reachable without braziers. Six actual normal create_run startup cases across all three modes also admit Engine and execute deterministic Wait after loading. Fifteen deliberate invalid inputs reject; invalid custom generator runs once, atomically.\n\nSource audit: bounded 8 complete-floor attempts × 32 geometry candidates; original world seed, domain/Godbeast plan and stairs retained. Failed candidates do not commit partial IDs/loot/metrics; no required content is silently omitted. Exhaustion is an explicit error, not an all-seed mathematical guarantee.\n\nFrozen 144 core/catalog/data input aggregate SHA256: {manifest['sha256']}\nInputs still match canonical source at receipt creation. Timings: {receipt['timings']}\n\nReproduction: compile core with Rust 1.99.1 optimized; rustc --edition=2024 -O stress.rs -L dependency=<release-deps> --extern corpse_core=<core.rlib> --extern serde_json=<serde_json.rlib> -o stress; ./stress 1024 38 4. Other harnesses compile likewise. Local corrected executable: generation-r38/independent-qa/corrected/stress-final.\n\nLimitations: sample, not exhaustive seed proof or complete playthroughs; DEBUG first-offer choices, not every build; no Windows runtime/desktop interaction. Lead owns workspace/Windows/archive gates. First-candidate interrupted-run evidence is preserved separately; final corrected corpus is a fresh full run.\n''';(dest/'REPORT.txt').write_text(report);print(json.dumps({'receipt':str(dest/'receipt.json'),'successful_worlds':1024,'fingerprint':manifest['sha256']}))
